SUMMARY:Noche De Liberación at Axelrad Beer Garden
DESCRIPTION:Workers Defense Project hosts Noche De Liberación\, an evening of community and solidarity with immigrant workers and families in Texas\, at Axelrad Beer Garden. \nAll are welcome to show up and enjoy music\, pizza\, lotería\, banner painting\, and a signature cocktail while spending time with neighbors and fellow supporters. \nFor every signature event cocktail ordered at the event\, Axelrad will donate $1 to Workers Defense. \nFamilies and all ages are welcome. Axelrad becomes 21+ only at 8pm. Axelrad’s Noches Calientes with Discoteka follows the event for ages 21+. \nThe fundraiser supports Workers Defense\, and donations are welcome at any time. \nAdmission\nFree. Learn more. \n \nThis Featured Calendar Listing was sponsored by the event organizer and boosted in our calendar with images and more details.  \nLearn more about promoting your event\, organization\, business\, or offer across all of our channels.
URL:https://365thingsinhouston.com/calendar/noche-de-liberacion-at-axelrad-beer-garden/
LOCATION:Axelrad Beer Garden\, 1517 Alabama St\, Houston\, TX\, 77004\, United States
CATEGORIES:Bars & Clubs,Boosted Calendar Listing,Clubs & Organizations,Community & Giving,Date Night,Drinks & Cocktails,Featured,Free,Fundraisers,History & Culture,Kids & Families,Live DJ,Mixers,Nonprofits,Outdoors,Parties,Pop-Ups
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://365thingsinhouston.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Noche-De-Liberacion-at-Axelrad-Beer-Garden.jpg
